<!--
  <summary>
  SETTINGS-HELP, 22/10/2026: the help text for the Skin Settings window,
  pulled in by Includes.xml. SettingsHelp maps whichever settings control
  has focus to one string saying what it does and, after a line break,
  where the thing it affects appears. settings_help_shown is true exactly
  when one of those controls has focus, so the panel in SkinSettings.xml
  hides rather than showing an empty box.
  </summary>
  <remarks>
  The strings are 31700 upwards in strings.po, one per control, except the
  eight main menu tiles, whose cycle, label and favourite rows share one
  string per kind of row. Two focusable controls are left out on purpose:
  7321, the one pixel relay focus passes through after the custom accent
  picker, and 7900, the unlabelled About strip, which help text would
  give away. A control added to SkinSettings.xml needs a value here and
  its id in settings_help_shown, or the panel stays hidden on it.
  </remarks>
-->
